  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "Why does a Death Order code say it is invalid?",
      "a": "Codes in Death Order are case-sensitive, so Home has to be typed with a capital H and the rest in lowercase. Each code also only works once per account, so a code you already used will fail the second time."
    },
    {
      "q": "What should I spend Death Order Cash on?",
      "a": "Cash buys prison suits and other cosmetics that change how your character looks. It does not make you better at following Simon's orders, so pick whatever style you like."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which Death Order code gives the most Cash?",
      "a": "MARLOWISHERE and CHACHING each give 5,000 Cash, while every other code gives 1,000. Redeem those two first before they expire."
    }
  ],
  "tips": [
    "Read each order fully before you move. If it does not start with Simon Says, the safest choice is to do nothing at all.",
    "Do not copy other players. If someone near you moves on a fake order and gets eliminated, following them only gets you out too.",
    "Set up your controls before you play. Settings lets you change PC keybinds, controller binds and the mobile HUD, which helps when later rounds need fast reactions.",
    "Later rounds come quicker, so take a breath and check the wording every time. Most mistakes happen when players react before reading."
  ],
  "useRewards": "All 15 working codes give Cash, adding up to 23,000 in total, with MARLOWISHERE and CHACHING worth 5,000 each. Cash goes toward prison suits and other looks, not power, so there is no rush to spend it. Redeem everything, then take your time browsing so you can pick an outfit you actually like instead of the first thing you can afford.",
